Create an SVG figure for the slide "3.5 Terminology: Hypa Hyper?" that shows
all terms of that slide at once, in a basic way. Same deck style as the other
figures (1200x675, white background, 'IBM Plex Sans' / 'Source Code Pro',
title in #8a0404, green = VM/guest, blue = VMM, purple = hypervisor,
grey = hardware).

Layered from top to bottom:
- Virtual Machine (VM): a virtual computer (vCPUs, memory, virtual devices),
  with the Guest inside it (OS kernel, drivers, user applications).
- Virtual Machine Monitor (VMM): unprivileged user-space program that creates
  the VM and emulates its virtual hardware; Cloud Hypervisor (CH), QEMU,
  VirtualBox; one VMM process per VM.
- Optional management software next to the VMM (libvirt, OpenStack, ...).
- A dashed frame around VMM + hypervisor + management software labelled
  "Virtualization stack".
- A dashed line separating user space (unprivileged) from kernel space
  (privileged).
- Hypervisor: privileged kernel component, isolation and resource management,
  uses the CPU extensions; Linux/KVM (/dev/kvm).
- Hardware: CPU with virtualization extensions (VMX / SVM), memory, devices.

Thin arrows: VMM provides the VM, VMM uses the hypervisor, hypervisor uses the
hardware.
